    "body": "Evaluating using `eval (..)` can produce problems depending on how the input is broken on newlines and how long the input is. Not that it may have those problems, but the input from `/dev/stdin` will *always* be taken as is, whereas evaluating command line arguments is more errorprone.\r\n\r\nTherefore, piping to `source` is the safest/most reliable option. Also, TIL you can pipe to `source`. I've been doing `source (cmd | psub)`, which also works, but is more indirect.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
