    "updated_at": "2019-10-14T11:21:23Z",
    "body": "> you should see that it's just source (starship init fish --print-full-init | psub)\r\n\r\nJust for fun I tested the perf impact calling starship twice during init on my system:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n❯ hyperfine -w 300 -m 1000 'starship init fish --print-full-init'\r\nBenchmark #1: starship init fish --print-full-init\r\n  Time (mean ± σ):       7.4 ms ±   0.8 ms    [User: 3.2 ms, System: 2.6 ms]\r\n  Range (min … max):     6.2 ms …  14.7 ms    1000 runs\r\n\r\n❯ hyperfine -w 300 -m 1000 'starship init fish'\r\nBenchmark #1: starship init fish\r\n  Time (mean ± σ):       7.4 ms ±   0.7 ms    [User: 3.2 ms, System: 2.5 ms]\r\n  Range (min … max):     6.0 ms …  11.9 ms    1000 runs\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhile fast there are ~14 ms that could be improved upon.\r\n\r\nDefault install instructions:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n❯ hyperfine -w 30 -m 100 'fish -i'\r\nBenchmark #1: fish -i\r\n  Time (mean ± σ):     112.9 ms ±   2.7 ms    [User: 60.3 ms, System: 58.4 ms]\r\n  Range (min … max):   108.4 ms … 131.6 ms    100 runs\r\n```\r\n\r\nI created a fish_prompt file with the contents of 'starship init fish --print-full-init' (not recommended for normal use)\r\n```\r\n❯ hyperfine -w 30 -m 100 'fish -i'\r\nBenchmark #1: fish -i\r\n  Time (mean ± σ):      96.8 ms ±   3.6 ms    [User: 51.4 ms, System: 50.2 ms]\r\n  Range (min … max):    90.1 ms … 111.5 ms    100 runs\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\nEdit:\r\nsidenote: I've got my shell down to 56 ms\r\n\r\n```\r\nBenchmark #1: fish -i\r\n  Time (mean ± σ):      56.1 ms ±   1.4 ms    [User: 30.0 ms, System: 24.8 ms]\r\n  Range (min … max):    54.2 ms …  62.4 ms    100 runs\r\n```",
